<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dardanus</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">In Greek mythology Dardanus was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeus">Zeus</a> and Electra, the founder of Dardania in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troad">Troad</a> and ancestor of the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troy">Troy</a>. Greek writers said he came to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samothrace">Samothrace</a>, while an Italian tradition, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virgil">Virgil</a>, made him a native of the Etruscan city of Corythus, usually identified with Cortona. Through him the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> could present <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aeneas">Aeneas</a>'s journey to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> as a homecoming.</p></div>
